  "status_text": "Even when a circuit may use NOT gates, some graphs keep their cost floor, and this evening's article tells two such floors whole. One of them, checked in Lean on one-a-side inputs: for every n by m graph with n and m at least 2, no two equal rows and no two equal columns, if no fan-in-two AND/OR circuit has at most n + m - 3 gates, then every fan-in-two AND/OR/NOT circuit has at least n + m - 2 [L-meta-25016].",
